    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2221" root="برد" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرْدَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَارِدٌ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  and see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرَدَةٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِىَ لَكَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرْدَةَ نَفْسَهَا</span> <i>She is purely thine;</i> (Fr, A'Obeyd, T,
S, M;) syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالِصَةً</span>: (M:) A'Obeyd explains it
by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَالِصًا</span>, (T, S, M,) not in the fem. form, (TA,)
on the authority of Fr. (T.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ لِى بَرْدَةَ يَمِينِى</span>,

(A'Obeyd, M,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ لِبَرْدَةِ يَمِينِى</span>, (S,) <i>He,</i> or
<i>it, is known to me.</i> (A'Obeyd, S, M.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرْدَةُ</span> a
proper name applied to <i>The ewe.</i> (K.)

